:EPANEL.
:PANEL NAME=WRKACTJI KEYL=SELKEYS HELP=WRKACTJI ENTER='RETURN 1' TOPSEP=SYSNAM.Include
:TOPINST.Type choices, press Enter.
:DATA DEPTH='*'.
:DATAI VAR=SELSBS USAGE=INOUT HELP='FLD/SELSBS'.Subsystem
:DATAI VAR=SELJOB USAGE=INOUT HELP='FLD/SELJOB'.Job name
:DATAI VAR=SELUSER USAGE=INOUT HELP='FLD/SELUSER'.Current user
:DATAI VAR=SELTYPE USAGE=INOUT HELP='FLD/SELTYPE'.Job type
:DATAI VAR=SELSTS USAGE=INOUT HELP='FLD/SELSTS'.Status
:EDATA.
:EPANEL.
:PANEL NAME=WRKACTJS KEYL=SELKEYS HELP=WRKACTJI ENTER='RETURN 1' TOPSEP=SYSNAM.Subset
:TOPINST.Type choices, press Enter.
:DATA DEPTH='*'.
:DATAI VAR=SELSBS USAGE=INOUT HELP='FLD/SELSBS'.Subsystem
:DATAI VAR=SELJOB USAGE=INOUT HELP='FLD/SELJOB'.Job name
:DATAI VAR=SELUSER USAGE=INOUT HELP='FLD/SELUSER'.Current user
:DATAI VAR=SELTYPE USAGE=INOUT HELP='FLD/SELTYPE'.Job type
:DATAI VAR=SELSTS USAGE=INOUT HELP='FLD/SELSTS'.Status
:EDATA.
:EPANEL.
:HELP NAME=WRKACTJ.Work with Active Jobs - Help
:P.Every job active on the system, under the subsystem it runs in.
Type an option next to a job to act on it, or a command on the
command line. F11 changes the columns shown; F5 measures again from
the last look; F10 starts the measurement over.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=WRKACTJI.Include and Subset - Help
:P.Which active jobs the list shows: a subsystem, a job name, the
current user, a job type (SBS, INT, BCH, ASJ, SYS, ...) or a status
(RUN, DEQW, ...); *ALL selects every one. A name may end in an
asterisk to select every name that starts with it. Include also brings
back the jobs option 9 left out.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=AJKEYS.Function keys
:P.F3 leaves the display, F5 refreshes it, F11 shows the next view and
F23 the other options. F24 shows the remaining keys.
:EHELP.
.* Item, key and option help.
:HELP NAME='FLD/SYSCPU'.CPU %
:P.The CPU % shown for what the display is about.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='WRKACTJ1/OPT'.Option
:P.Type the number of an option next to an entry and press Enter. The
options the list allows are shown above it; F1 on one of them explains
it.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/JOB'.Subsystem/Job
:P.The subsystem/Job of each entry in the list.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/CURUSER'.Current User
:P.The current User of each entry in the list.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/USER'.User
:P.The user of each entry in the list.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/NUMBER'.Number
:P.The number of each entry in the list.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/TYPE'.Type
:P.The type of each entry in the list.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/CPU'.CPU %
:P.The CPU % of each entry in the list.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/FUNCTION'.Function
:P.The function of each entry in the list.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/STATUS'.Status
:P.The status of each entry in the list.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/POOL'.Pool
:P.The pool of each entry in the list.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/PTY'.Pty
:P.The pty of each entry in the list.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/CPUSEC'.CPU
:P.The CPU of each entry in the list.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/INT'.--------Elapsed--------- int
:P.The --------Elapsed--------- int of each entry in the list.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/RSP'.--------Elapsed--------- rsp
:P.The --------Elapsed--------- rsp of each entry in the list.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/AUXIO'.--------Elapsed--------- auxIO
:P.The --------Elapsed--------- auxIO of each entry in the list.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/ECPU'.--------Elapsed--------- CPU %
:P.The --------Elapsed--------- CPU % of each entry in the list.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/THREADS'.Threads
:P.The threads of each entry in the list.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/TMPSTG'.Temporary Storage
:P.The temporary Storage of each entry in the list.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='WRKACTJ1/OPTIONS'.Options
:P.Type an option number next to one or more entries and press Enter.
The option runs for each entry it is typed next to, in order.
:PARML.
:PT.2=Change
:PD.Type 2 next to an entry and press Enter to change it. The Change Job
(CHGJOB) command is prompted for the entry.
:PT.3=Hold
:PD.Type 3 next to an entry and press Enter to hold it. The Hold Job
(HLDJOB) command runs for the entry.
:PT.4=End
:PD.Type 4 next to an entry and press Enter to end it. The End Job
(ENDJOB) command is prompted for the entry.
:PT.5=Work with
:PD.Type 5 next to an entry and press Enter to work with it. The Work
with Job (WRKJOB) command runs for the entry.
:PT.6=Release
:PD.Type 6 next to an entry and press Enter to release it. The Release
Job (RLSJOB) command runs for the entry.
:PT.7=Display message
:PD.Type 7 next to an entry and press Enter to display message it. The
Display Job Log (DSPJOBLOG) command runs for the entry.
:PT.8=Work with spooled files
:PD.Type 8 next to an entry and press Enter to work with spooled files
it. The Work with Job (WRKJOB) command runs for the entry.
:PT.13=Disconnect ...
:PD.Type 13 next to an entry and press Enter to disconnect &period...
it. The Disconnect Job (DSCJOB) command runs for the entry.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='WRKACTJ2/OPT'.Option
:P.Type the number of an option next to an entry and press Enter. The
options the list allows are shown above it; F1 on one of them explains
it.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='WRKACTJ2/OPTIONS'.Options
:P.Type an option number next to one or more entries and press Enter.
The option runs for each entry it is typed next to, in order.
:PARML.
:PT.9=Exclude
:PD.Type 9 next to an entry and press Enter to exclude it.
:PT.10=Display call stack
:PD.Type 10 next to an entry and press Enter to display call stack it.
The Work with Job (WRKJOB) command runs for the entry.
:PT.11=Work with locks
:PD.Type 11 next to an entry and press Enter to work with locks it. The
Work with Job (WRKJOB) command runs for the entry.
:PT.12=Work with threads
:PD.Type 12 next to an entry and press Enter to work with threads it.
The Work with Job (WRKJOB) command runs for the entry.
:PT.14=Work with mutexes ...
:PD.Type 14 next to an entry and press Enter to work with mutexes
&period... it. The Work with Job (WRKJOB) command runs for the entry.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='WRKACTJW/OPT'.Option
:P.Type the number of an option next to an entry and press Enter. The
options the list allows are shown above it; F1 on one of them explains
it.
:EHELP.
