:PT.8=Work with spooled files
:PD.Type 8 next to an entry and press Enter to work with spooled files
it. The Work with Job (WRKJOB) command runs for the entry.
:PT.9=Exclude
:PD.Type 9 next to an entry and press Enter to exclude it.
:PT.10=Display call stack
:PD.Type 10 next to an entry and press Enter to display call stack it.
The Work with Job (WRKJOB) command runs for the entry.
:PT.11=Work with locks
:PD.Type 11 next to an entry and press Enter to work with locks it. The
Work with Job (WRKJOB) command runs for the entry.
:PT.12=Work with threads
:PD.Type 12 next to an entry and press Enter to work with threads it.
The Work with Job (WRKJOB) command runs for the entry.
:PT.13=Disconnect
:PD.Type 13 next to an entry and press Enter to disconnect it. The
Disconnect Job (DSCJOB) command runs for the entry.
:PT.14=Work with mutexes
:PD.Type 14 next to an entry and press Enter to work with mutexes it.
The Work with Job (WRKJOB) command runs for the entry.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='KEYS/SELKEYS'.Function keys
:PARML.
:PT.F3=Exit
:PD.Ends the display and returns to where it was started from.
:PT.F5=Refresh
:PD.Shows the display again with the current information.
:PT.F12=Cancel
:PD.Returns to the previous display without acting on what was typed.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/SELSBS'.Subsystem
:P.Type the subsystem.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/SELJOB'.Job name
:P.The job, by name, user and number. A job name alone is enough when
only one job has it.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/SELUSER'.Current user
:P.Type the current user.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/SELTYPE'.Job type
:P.Type the job type.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/SELSTS'.Status
:P.Type the status.
:EHELP.
:EPNLGRP.
